; Program 4.15: y = sum of kⁿ for k = 1..m
; Source: Дьяконов, «Справочник по расчётам на микрокалькуляторах», 1985, p.67-68 (book61.pdf pages 68-69)
; Input: m in X, С/П; then n in X, С/П.  Output: y in X.
; Fxʸ is used with the base k in X and the exponent n in Y.
;
; Book example: m = 20, n = 4 -> y = 722665,91 (exact value 722666; the printed
; value carries the 8-digit error of xʸ)
; @input 20
; @input 4
; @expect X=722665.91 tol=1e-5
; @reset
; expected value computed, not printed in the book: m = 5, n = 2 -> 55
; @input 5
; @input 2
; @expect X=55 tol=1e-6
;
00: П7 С/П П9 0 П4 П8 КИП4 ИП4 ИП9 ↔
10: Fxʸ ИП8 + П8 ИП7 ИП4 − Fx=0 06 ИП8
20: С/П БП 00
